WEBVTT

00:00:26.090 --> 00:00:28.745
The lizard men will no longer
be subject to rat oppression!

00:00:30.747 --> 00:00:31.748
Aw, they're not oppressed.

00:00:31.791 --> 00:00:32.836
We raise them as food.

00:00:32.879 --> 00:00:33.837
They-they like it.

00:00:33.880 --> 00:00:35.230
Well, we are delicious.

00:00:35.273 --> 00:00:37.580
No. You should be free to do
whatever you want.

00:00:37.623 --> 00:00:40.713
-What do lizards like to do?
-Mm, bask?

00:00:40.757 --> 00:00:43.586
Okay. Then you should bask
without fear of being eaten.

00:00:43.629 --> 00:00:44.848
Well, that does sounds nice.

00:00:44.891 --> 00:00:46.415
This will not stand!

00:00:46.458 --> 00:00:48.504
Buddy, my captain's on the way
right now.

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:50.941
It's funny. Normally, I'm, like,a huge disappointment to her,

00:00:50.984 --> 00:00:52.334
but this time
she's gonna be pumped

00:00:52.377 --> 00:00:54.118
that I rooted out injustice.

00:00:54.162 --> 00:00:55.467
And here comes the praise,

00:00:55.511 --> 00:00:57.382
-in five...
-Attention, everyone.

00:00:57.426 --> 00:01:00.298
I'm afraid my ensign
has made a huge mistake.

00:01:00.342 --> 00:01:01.995
-What?
-Starfleet is forbidden

00:01:02.039 --> 00:01:04.172
from interfering
in your planetary politics.

00:01:04.215 --> 00:01:06.174
You will be free
to determine your future

00:01:06.217 --> 00:01:07.958
without our influence.

00:01:08.001 --> 00:01:11.048
What? How could you--
Oh, screw the Prime Directive!

00:01:12.093 --> 00:01:13.050
Hey.

00:01:13.094 --> 00:01:14.878
You are way out of bounds here.

00:01:14.921 --> 00:01:16.097
They're eatingthose guys.

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.228
What am I supposed to do?

00:01:17.272 --> 00:01:18.708
Report it to me.

00:01:18.751 --> 00:01:21.319
Now I have to explain why
there's an interspecies war

00:01:21.363 --> 00:01:23.669
on a planet
that was peaceful yesterday!

00:01:23.713 --> 00:01:25.758
Oh, so you're yelling at me
for spreading freedom

00:01:25.802 --> 00:01:27.978
because you don't feel
like filing a report?

00:01:29.327 --> 00:01:31.721
Mariner, I swear,
if you weren't my daughter,

00:01:31.764 --> 00:01:33.157
you'd be off the Cerritos.

00:01:33.201 --> 00:01:34.419
If I wasn't your daughter,

00:01:34.463 --> 00:01:35.899
you wouldn't be such a bitch
all the time!

00:01:35.942 --> 00:01:37.814
That's it. That's it!
When we get back to the ship,

00:01:37.857 --> 00:01:39.816
-you are going straight to...
-Yeah, yeah, I know.

00:01:39.859 --> 00:01:41.383
Straight to the brig.
Shocker.

00:01:41.426 --> 00:01:43.428
Oh, you're not going
to the brig.

00:01:43.472 --> 00:01:45.300
You're going to therapy.

00:01:45.343 --> 00:01:47.737
What?!
You think Ineed therapy?

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:49.086
What? That's-- No!

00:01:49.130 --> 00:01:50.218
It's the '80s, dude.

00:01:50.261 --> 00:01:51.784
We don't have
psychiatric problems.

00:01:51.828 --> 00:01:53.177
You're a loose cannon.

00:01:53.221 --> 00:01:55.179
I don't care
how many lizards you save.

00:01:55.223 --> 00:01:57.442
You need professional help.

00:01:57.486 --> 00:02:00.271
Dr. Migleemo? Oh, he's the
worst counselor in the fleet!

00:02:00.315 --> 00:02:02.882
He just tosses out
nonstop food metaphors!

00:02:02.926 --> 00:02:04.275
That's an order, Ensign.

00:02:04.319 --> 00:02:05.494
Freeman to Cerritos.

00:02:05.537 --> 00:02:06.495
-One to beam up.

00:02:06.538 --> 00:02:08.453
I don't need therapy!

00:02:09.498 --> 00:02:11.848
Okay, look,
will you stop eating these guys

00:02:11.891 --> 00:02:13.589
if we give you food replicators?

00:02:13.632 --> 00:02:15.721
Ha. I don't know.
Can they make nutrient pellets?

00:02:15.765 --> 00:02:16.983
Yes!

00:03:28.446 --> 00:03:30.361
Mariner,
this report is

00:03:30.405 --> 00:03:33.408
a veritable fruit salad
of insubordination.

00:03:33.451 --> 00:03:34.757
I don't want to be here.
I broke the rules.

00:03:34.800 --> 00:03:36.237
I'm supposed to be in the brig.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:37.455
Sorry.
Captain's orders.

00:03:37.499 --> 00:03:39.544
She wants us to meet every week,

00:03:39.588 --> 00:03:41.198
cooking up
some healthy strategies

00:03:41.242 --> 00:03:44.462
to marinate you into the officershe knows you can be.

00:03:44.506 --> 00:03:45.681
I don't want your help!

00:03:45.724 --> 00:03:46.856
I want to show the captain
that she's wrong

00:03:46.899 --> 00:03:48.858
and then get put...
in... the... brig!

00:03:48.901 --> 00:03:50.686
Full stop, Beckett.

00:03:50.729 --> 00:03:53.254
We need to find an outlet
for all that rage.

00:03:53.297 --> 00:03:55.256
Have you ever made paella?

00:03:57.388 --> 00:03:59.347
Nice shot, da Vinci!

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:01.131
-Grazie.
-Hey, guys.

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.132
Do you mind
if I take over the deck?

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.307
I've got a big evaluation

00:04:03.351 --> 00:04:04.613
with Captain Freeman
this afternoon.

00:04:04.656 --> 00:04:06.049
She's selecting
eager to please candidates

00:04:06.092 --> 00:04:07.659
for her advanced diplomacy
workshop.

00:04:07.703 --> 00:04:09.748
Problem is, I don't know
howeager to please.

00:04:09.792 --> 00:04:11.315
Ugh, I got to practice.

00:04:11.359 --> 00:04:13.796
Computer,
load program Boimler seven.

00:04:13.839 --> 00:04:16.189
-Ciao, da Vinci.
-Ciao, Tendi.

00:04:19.236 --> 00:04:21.325
Ugh, you simulated the crew?

00:04:21.369 --> 00:04:22.892
Yeah, that way,
I can pre-interview

00:04:22.935 --> 00:04:24.894
so I don't make any mistakes
when it's for real.

00:04:24.937 --> 00:04:26.461
I uploaded
seven years of entries

00:04:26.504 --> 00:04:27.984
from the entire crew's
private logs...

00:04:28.027 --> 00:04:29.072
Aren't those private?

00:04:29.115 --> 00:04:30.595
...and it
algorithmically created

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:32.641
a perfect simulation
of everyone on the Cerritos.

00:04:32.684 --> 00:04:35.383
They'll respond exactly the way
they would in real life.

00:04:35.426 --> 00:04:36.384
Ah.

00:04:36.427 --> 00:04:37.472
Hey, buddy.
How's it going?

00:04:37.515 --> 00:04:39.125
Don't talk to me!
I'm pissed off!

00:04:39.169 --> 00:04:42.041
Whoa! Amazing! We had that exactsame conversation an hour ago.

00:04:42.085 --> 00:04:45.001
Yeah. Ah. All I got to do
is feed it a scenario.

00:04:45.044 --> 00:04:47.569
Then the simulated crew
fills in the blanks.

00:04:47.612 --> 00:04:49.310
It'll give me an edge
in my interview.

00:04:50.354 --> 00:04:51.790
-Ahoy, Cap'n.
-"Ahoy"?

00:04:51.834 --> 00:04:54.184
See? I just learned
not to say that.

00:04:54.227 --> 00:04:56.360
Congrats on the brownnosing
program, butt-kisser.

00:04:56.404 --> 00:04:58.057
Only you would-- Wait.

00:04:58.101 --> 00:05:00.233
This is a perfectsimulation?

00:05:01.539 --> 00:05:02.497
What was that?

00:05:02.540 --> 00:05:03.672
Hey, hey,
what are you doing?

00:05:03.715 --> 00:05:05.674
"Interior.
Rickety metal catwalk. Night"?

00:05:05.717 --> 00:05:07.502
Mariner! You can't write that
about the captain.

00:05:07.545 --> 00:05:09.504
Why waste this
on some dumb interview prep?

00:05:09.547 --> 00:05:11.506
-I'm putting in
my own parameters.
-If Freeman sees this,

00:05:11.549 --> 00:05:12.550
you'll get court-martialed.

00:05:12.594 --> 00:05:13.551
What did she ever do to you?

00:05:13.595 --> 00:05:14.552
You say I need therapy?

00:05:14.596 --> 00:05:15.901
Okay, I'll go to therapy.

00:05:15.945 --> 00:05:17.729
Mariner, don't touch my code!
Don't touch my...

00:05:17.773 --> 00:05:19.470
Therapy...!

00:05:20.993 --> 00:05:23.169
What the hell?
What did you do to my program?

00:05:23.213 --> 00:05:24.649
I made it
into an awesome movie.

00:05:24.693 --> 00:05:26.651
Oh, I'm gonna work
some  out.

00:05:28.044 --> 00:05:29.480
-: All right!

00:05:29.524 --> 00:05:31.177
-Ooh, nice font.

00:05:31.221 --> 00:05:33.484
No, no, what are
you talking about? A movie?

00:05:33.528 --> 00:05:35.747
What, you wrote out
a whole script in two seconds?

00:05:35.791 --> 00:05:37.967
-I just, like,
hit the act breaks,

00:05:38.010 --> 00:05:39.621
-couple set pieces.
-Set pieces?

00:05:39.664 --> 00:05:40.796
The computer's
filling in the rest.

00:05:40.839 --> 00:05:42.363
I made parts for the crew
and all of us!

00:05:42.406 --> 00:05:43.364
It's gonna be great!

00:05:43.407 --> 00:05:45.583
I don't want to do a movie!

00:05:45.627 --> 00:05:47.280
That's okay. You were
kind of a Xon, to be honest.

00:05:47.324 --> 00:05:48.586
You probably weren't gonna make
final cut.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:50.414
-Who's Xon?
-Exactly.

00:05:50.458 --> 00:05:51.937
Ooh, I've always wanted
to be in a movie!

00:05:51.981 --> 00:05:53.156
Can I be the voice of the ship?

00:05:53.199 --> 00:05:54.636
"Red alert! Red alert!"

00:05:54.679 --> 00:05:56.202
No, no, I got
the perfect part for you.

00:05:56.246 --> 00:05:57.595
-You're gonna love it.
-Guys!

00:05:57.639 --> 00:05:59.205
This is an important work tool,

00:05:59.249 --> 00:06:00.772
not a fun thing
to have a good time with.

00:06:00.816 --> 00:06:02.600
Boimler, pipe down. Shh.
Come on, the credits.

00:06:02.644 --> 00:06:04.036
I don't want this.

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.429
-I just want to prep.
-Well, tough.

00:06:05.473 --> 00:06:06.952
You're just gonna have to wait
till it's over.

00:06:06.996 --> 00:06:08.780
Come on, come on, come on,
let's go get into costume.

00:06:08.824 --> 00:06:09.868
-Okeydokey!

00:06:09.912 --> 00:06:11.043
I'm not getting in anything.

00:06:11.087 --> 00:06:13.655
Mariner!
I want these credits gone now!

00:06:13.698 --> 00:06:15.047
-Hmm.

00:06:15.091 --> 00:06:17.180
Wha?

00:06:20.531 --> 00:06:21.445
Yeah!

00:06:21.489 --> 00:06:23.099
Happy birthday, Captain!

00:06:23.142 --> 00:06:24.840
I might be getting up in years,

00:06:24.883 --> 00:06:27.233
but I still hold
the hydroscoot speed record

00:06:27.277 --> 00:06:28.496
back at the Academy!

00:06:28.539 --> 00:06:30.889
-Captain out!


-RANSOM: Whoa!

00:06:30.933 --> 00:06:32.413
-Get him, Captain!

00:06:32.456 --> 00:06:33.414
Shut up!

00:06:33.457 --> 00:06:34.806
I'll kill you! I--

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.982
Oh, I can't stay mad.

00:06:39.071 --> 00:06:40.464
Good one, Cap'n!

00:06:40.508 --> 00:06:41.465
I don't remember
giving you permission

00:06:41.509 --> 00:06:42.684
to scoot with us, Ensign.

00:06:42.727 --> 00:06:44.163
Yeah, actually, I need to
borrow the cap'n

00:06:44.207 --> 00:06:46.209
-for a quick interview.
-It's her birthday!

00:06:46.252 --> 00:06:47.558
Um, can I at least ask
what she likes more,

00:06:47.602 --> 00:06:50.474
when bridge officers
arrive early or stay late?

00:06:50.518 --> 00:06:51.997
A question like that
makes me think

00:06:52.041 --> 00:06:54.173
you're asking
the wrong questions.

00:06:54.217 --> 00:06:55.566
Good... to... know.

00:06:55.610 --> 00:06:56.741
Sorry to interrupt
your vacation.

00:06:56.785 --> 00:06:58.264
This isn't a vacation.

00:06:58.308 --> 00:07:00.441
-It's important
scientific research.

00:07:00.484 --> 00:07:02.747
Vacation's over.

00:07:03.835 --> 00:07:05.968
VASSERY: Sorry for the short
notice, Captain Freeman.

00:07:06.011 --> 00:07:07.491
Not a problem at all, Admiral.

00:07:07.535 --> 00:07:09.362
-How can we help?
-We've received
a bizarre message

00:07:09.406 --> 00:07:10.886
from the leaders of Idlocana 6.

00:07:10.929 --> 00:07:12.496
Their president
wanted to thank us

00:07:12.540 --> 00:07:14.019
for a wonderful second contact

00:07:14.063 --> 00:07:15.499
with the crew
of the San Clemente.

00:07:15.543 --> 00:07:16.892
So? What's wrong with that?

00:07:16.935 --> 00:07:19.721
Starfleet doesn't have
a San Clemente.

00:07:19.764 --> 00:07:23.507
Whoever second-contacted them
wasn't our ship.

00:07:23.551 --> 00:07:24.987
What a mystery.

00:07:25.030 --> 00:07:26.510
Uh, whose boy is this?

00:07:26.554 --> 00:07:27.772
Ensign Brad Boimler, sir.

00:07:27.816 --> 00:07:29.644
Here to learn.

00:07:29.687 --> 00:07:31.036
This impostor--

00:07:31.080 --> 00:07:33.038
you want
the Cerritosto investigate?

00:07:33.082 --> 00:07:35.301
Get in, get me intel,
then get out.

00:07:35.345 --> 00:07:37.608
And, Freeman,
stick to the plan this time.

00:07:37.652 --> 00:07:40.132
If this was actually happening,
they'd send the Enterprise.

00:07:40.176 --> 00:07:41.917
But, you know,
artistic license.

00:07:41.960 --> 00:07:44.397
Luckily, the Cerritosjust went through some upgrades.

00:07:44.441 --> 00:07:47.662
We should be more than suitable
for the task.

00:07:49.751 --> 00:07:52.580
The Cerritosis ready
to launch whenever you are.

00:07:52.623 --> 00:07:54.146
Oh.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:55.713
There she is.

00:08:51.203 --> 00:08:53.945
She never fails
to take my breath away.

00:08:53.989 --> 00:08:56.513
-I wish I could kiss her
and squeeze her.
-Excuse me?

00:08:56.557 --> 00:08:59.603
Uh, uh, the Cerritos
is a handsome lady.

00:08:59.647 --> 00:09:01.692
You're damn right
about that, Boimler.

00:09:01.736 --> 00:09:05.566
Call the ship a handsome lady.

00:09:14.836 --> 00:09:16.751
Hmm.

00:09:18.230 --> 00:09:21.407
Captain,
we're ready for your command.

00:09:21.451 --> 00:09:24.715
Mm, time to take this puppy
off its leash.

00:09:42.994 --> 00:09:44.866
The selenium rings aredisrupting the sensors, Captain.

00:09:44.909 --> 00:09:46.868
I'm not detecting
any Federation...

00:09:46.911 --> 00:09:48.521
Hold on.

00:09:48.565 --> 00:09:50.480
-Enemy vessel decloaking!
-Raise shields!

00:09:54.963 --> 00:09:58.575
Like a rat to the bait, Freeman.

00:09:58.619 --> 00:10:01.578
Predictable as always.

00:10:01.622 --> 00:10:03.711
-Who is this marauder, Captain?
-I don't know.

00:10:03.754 --> 00:10:07.105
I am Vindicta,
vengeance personified!

00:10:07.149 --> 00:10:08.890
At last, Freeman.

00:10:08.933 --> 00:10:11.370
I will bathe in your blood.

00:10:11.414 --> 00:10:13.634
Oh, boy, somebody's
really laying it on thick.

00:10:13.677 --> 00:10:16.637
Behold my three henchmen
of the apo...

00:10:16.680 --> 00:10:18.551
of the Vin-pocalypse.

00:10:18.595 --> 00:10:21.467
Tendi, my savage warrior queen

00:10:21.511 --> 00:10:26.255
who comes from a long line
of thieving Orion pirates.

00:10:26.298 --> 00:10:28.692
Yeah, nobody messes with Orions.

00:10:28.736 --> 00:10:31.826
I'll steal from anyone
and never give it back. Theft!

00:10:31.869 --> 00:10:33.305
And, uh,

00:10:33.349 --> 00:10:34.698
B-Bionic 5,

00:10:34.742 --> 00:10:37.745
half man-meat,
half robot-meat, all pain.

00:10:37.788 --> 00:10:39.964
100% pain.

00:10:40.008 --> 00:10:44.099
Tremble at the sight
of the great Vindicta!

00:10:44.142 --> 00:10:45.840
And Shempo.

00:10:45.883 --> 00:10:49.017
I'm Shempo. I was supposed
to be played by Boimler.

00:10:49.060 --> 00:10:50.801
Okay, come on.
I don't sound like that.

00:10:50.845 --> 00:10:53.456
I love my captain, and I don't
want to be doing this.

00:10:53.499 --> 00:10:55.240
All right,
that's not too far off.

00:10:55.284 --> 00:10:57.460
You're posing as Starfleet. Why?

00:10:57.503 --> 00:11:00.071
Because I do what I want!
Ugh, you're a jerk, Freeman.

00:11:00.115 --> 00:11:02.291
You're nothing
but a propped up errand girl,

00:11:02.334 --> 00:11:05.773
blindly licking Starfleet's boot and begging for heel.

00:11:05.816 --> 00:11:07.905
Oh! Vindicta got your ass.

00:11:07.949 --> 00:11:10.342
Look, there's no need
for theatrics, all right?

00:11:10.386 --> 00:11:13.345
-I'm sure you're a reasonable...-Shempo got you tea, master.

00:11:13.389 --> 00:11:15.739
This is coffee!

00:11:15.783 --> 00:11:17.567
I was Shempo.

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:19.221
-That poor Shempo!

00:11:19.264 --> 00:11:21.527
You didn't have to do that.
Are you out of your mind?

00:11:21.571 --> 00:11:23.747
Freeman, you disgust me.

00:11:23.791 --> 00:11:25.967
You're a coward
who hides behind rank.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.403
You can't even appreciate

00:11:27.446 --> 00:11:29.100
your most valuable,
creative thinkers.

00:11:29.144 --> 00:11:31.363
I am Vindicta! Today you die.

00:11:31.407 --> 00:11:33.583
This Vindicta
is all over the place.

00:11:33.626 --> 00:11:35.585
"Hell is empty,
and all the devils are here.

00:11:35.628 --> 00:11:37.935
Our revels now are ended."

00:11:37.979 --> 00:11:39.937
Wait,
is she quoting The Tempest?

00:11:43.593 --> 00:11:45.595
"Hell is empty,
and all the devils are...

00:11:45.638 --> 00:11:47.205
"Hell is empty,
and all the devils

00:11:47.249 --> 00:11:48.598
-are here."
-FREEMAN: Wait,
this is a recording.

00:11:48.641 --> 00:11:50.252
It's a distraction.

00:11:50.295 --> 00:11:51.688
Winger?

00:11:51.732 --> 00:11:53.342
Hi. I'm Lieutenant Lemonts.

00:11:53.385 --> 00:11:55.779
Your one-man show
took my breath away.

00:11:55.823 --> 00:11:57.172
Thank you. Thank...

00:12:02.917 --> 00:12:05.354
Freeman! Bring me Free...

00:12:06.703 --> 00:12:08.966
-God, these stupid capes.
So much fabric.

00:12:12.578 --> 00:12:15.364
Bring me Freeman,
and I'll let you live.

00:12:15.407 --> 00:12:16.713
Never, witch!

00:12:18.410 --> 00:12:19.803
RUTHERFORD:
Wow.

00:12:19.847 --> 00:12:21.022
Boimler did a good job.

00:12:21.065 --> 00:12:22.458
Chief Lundy's accent
was spot-on.

00:12:22.501 --> 00:12:24.286
Yeah, and the way his face
was all blotchy?

00:12:24.329 --> 00:12:26.767
-Wait, do you think
Billups is in here?
-Eh, probably.

00:12:26.810 --> 00:12:29.117
So I can say
whatever I want to my boss

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.988
with no consequences?

00:12:33.164 --> 00:12:35.732
-Hey, wait! We have to hench!
-Tendi, come on.

00:12:35.776 --> 00:12:37.212
Pirate it up. Take some slaves.

00:12:37.255 --> 00:12:40.389
Oh, uh, you know the whole
"Orions taking slaves" thing?

00:12:40.432 --> 00:12:42.434
It's not something
I really like to...

00:12:42.478 --> 00:12:44.088
-Dirty Orion.

00:12:44.132 --> 00:12:45.133
Lundy!

00:12:48.397 --> 00:12:51.095
Give me Freeman!

00:12:51.139 --> 00:12:53.619
Attack formation Raptor.

00:12:53.663 --> 00:12:55.491
This isn't my first
overpowered space warlord,

00:12:55.534 --> 00:12:57.493
and it won't be my last.

00:12:59.495 --> 00:13:01.758
Ransom,you think you're better than me?

00:13:01.802 --> 00:13:03.847
Better at being
the captain's little dick wig.

00:13:03.891 --> 00:13:05.980
You can talk the talk,
but can you... Ow!

00:13:06.023 --> 00:13:07.677
--Walk the walk! She can do both!

00:13:07.720 --> 00:13:09.635
-Oh, she's walkin' and talkin'.
-Sir, quick,

00:13:09.679 --> 00:13:11.855
-what's the captain's
favorite type of cookie?
-What?!

00:13:11.899 --> 00:13:13.552
Tell me
before you succumb to the pain.

00:13:13.596 --> 00:13:14.858
If I were to bake her cookies,

00:13:14.902 --> 00:13:16.991
-what would be my best bet?

00:13:17.034 --> 00:13:19.384
Cap's got a sweet tooth.
Cookies are a good move.

00:13:19.428 --> 00:13:21.473
I've done it myself.
But watch out.

00:13:21.517 --> 00:13:23.519
She's allergic to...

00:13:24.825 --> 00:13:26.261
Allergic to what? Ransom!

00:13:26.304 --> 00:13:28.872
Allergic to what?!

00:13:28.916 --> 00:13:30.265
At your stations, people.

00:13:30.308 --> 00:13:31.657
This is not a drill.

00:13:31.701 --> 00:13:34.573
Billups! Show yourself!

00:13:34.617 --> 00:13:35.792
Sir, get down!

00:13:40.057 --> 00:13:41.058
Engineering, evacuate!

00:13:44.148 --> 00:13:45.933
Andy Billups!

00:13:45.976 --> 00:13:49.023
You think you're
the best engineer in the fleet.

00:13:49.066 --> 00:13:50.720
Well, I've wanted
to say something to you

00:13:50.763 --> 00:13:53.070
for a long time.

00:13:53.114 --> 00:13:54.898
You arethe best engineer
in the fleet!

00:13:54.942 --> 00:13:57.335
-Huh?
-I love how
you program subroutines.

00:13:57.379 --> 00:13:58.554
It's breathtaking.

00:13:58.597 --> 00:14:00.817
It feels so good to say it.

00:14:00.861 --> 00:14:02.819
COMPUTER: Warning. Hydron levels critical.

00:14:02.863 --> 00:14:04.386
Damn it!
We don't have much time.

00:14:04.429 --> 00:14:06.692
Rerouting the vent system
would take a whole team.

00:14:06.736 --> 00:14:08.172
If we bypass the indacontrols

00:14:08.216 --> 00:14:09.304
and suppress the sativents,

00:14:09.347 --> 00:14:10.740
it should function as a...

00:14:10.783 --> 00:14:12.568
BOTH:
Rudimentary plasma filter.

00:14:12.611 --> 00:14:15.658
Wow,
for a random space marauder,

00:14:15.701 --> 00:14:17.790
you really know your way
around a starship.

00:14:17.834 --> 00:14:19.096
Aw, thanks.

00:14:20.141 --> 00:14:21.882
SHAXS:
Intruder!

00:14:22.883 --> 00:14:24.232
When you get to hell,

00:14:24.275 --> 00:14:26.234
tell the Pah-wraiths
that Shaxs sent you!

00:14:26.277 --> 00:14:28.976
Special delivery
straight from Bajor!

00:14:30.020 --> 00:14:31.152
Ah, shut up.

00:14:39.116 --> 00:14:41.075
Borg head?

00:14:41.118 --> 00:14:43.381
-Designation: explosive.

00:14:46.602 --> 00:14:48.212
-Oh, look!

00:14:48.256 --> 00:14:50.475
Oh, Shaxs's earring.
You have to wear it.

00:14:50.519 --> 00:14:52.129
-Come here. Come here.
-Uh, I-I don't know.

00:14:52.173 --> 00:14:53.435
Isn't there, like,
religious significance?

00:14:53.478 --> 00:14:55.176
I mean,
some of his ear's still on it.

00:14:55.219 --> 00:14:57.004
Come on, dude.
Orions are pirates!

00:14:57.047 --> 00:14:58.309
Pillaging's your whole thing.

00:14:58.353 --> 00:15:00.964
Okay, stop!
It is not mywhole thing.

00:15:01.008 --> 00:15:03.227
And for your information,many Orions haven't been pirates

00:15:03.271 --> 00:15:05.012
for over five years!

00:15:05.055 --> 00:15:08.276
Okay, sorry. Look, you can just
be my generic warrior henchman.

00:15:08.319 --> 00:15:10.452
Come on! Come on,let's go torture the cat doctor.

00:15:10.495 --> 00:15:11.975
Like, really torture
the hell out of her.

00:15:12.019 --> 00:15:13.542
Her name is Dr. T'Ana.

00:15:13.585 --> 00:15:16.197
You're waytoo into this.
This is messed up.

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:18.112
MARINER:
It's the holodeck.
It's not real.

00:15:18.155 --> 00:15:20.114
-Die! Die!

00:15:21.942 --> 00:15:24.683
What is with you today?
This is not healthy.

00:15:24.727 --> 00:15:26.250
-Can we stop the movie?
-No!

00:15:26.294 --> 00:15:27.773
No, I'm fine.
This is feeling good.

00:15:27.817 --> 00:15:29.123
Come on, let me
just take down the captain,

00:15:29.166 --> 00:15:30.428
and then we can grab tacos.

00:15:30.472 --> 00:15:32.256
I don't want to watch you
phaser the captain.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:34.128
Phaser?

00:15:34.171 --> 00:15:37.348
Oh, it's going to be wayworse
than that.

00:15:37.392 --> 00:15:39.742
I am out of here. Arch.

00:15:39.785 --> 00:15:41.613
MARINER:
Hey, come on.

00:15:41.657 --> 00:15:43.224
This isn't you.

00:15:43.267 --> 00:15:44.660
It is, too!

00:15:48.185 --> 00:15:50.883
Ransom. Shaxs. Anyone, come in.

00:15:52.624 --> 00:15:55.671
No one left to hide behind,
Captain.

00:15:55.714 --> 00:15:58.500
It's just me and you.

00:15:58.543 --> 00:15:59.936
And-and these guys.

00:16:04.245 --> 00:16:05.724
You'll never take my ship.

00:16:05.768 --> 00:16:07.335
I don't want your ship.

00:16:07.378 --> 00:16:09.293
I want you to stop treating me

00:16:09.337 --> 00:16:10.903
like I'm the bad guy
all the time.

00:16:10.947 --> 00:16:12.166
You arethe bad guy.

00:16:12.209 --> 00:16:14.820
No, I'm not.Why don't you ever side with me?

00:16:14.864 --> 00:16:16.257
I don't even know you.

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.867
Exactly!

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:20.522
Oh, my God. You're-you're crazy.

00:16:20.565 --> 00:16:23.394
-No, thisis crazy.

00:16:23.438 --> 00:16:25.179
Sir, her ship.

00:16:25.222 --> 00:16:27.311
-The warp core's gone critical.
-Brace for impact!

00:17:01.084 --> 00:17:02.738
-COMPUTER: Warning. Warning.

00:17:02.781 --> 00:17:06.307
- -The ship has crashed. Warning.

00:17:11.747 --> 00:17:14.054
Oh, damn it.

00:17:16.317 --> 00:17:18.928
All surviving crew,
emergency evacuation protocol:

00:17:18.971 --> 00:17:20.930
Delta Echo.

00:17:20.973 --> 00:17:23.280
I'll keep systems functional
for as long as possible.

00:17:23.324 --> 00:17:26.022
You can do this.
Wecan do this.

00:17:26.066 --> 00:17:27.763
-Cerritosstrong!

00:17:27.806 --> 00:17:29.504
Oh, when are you going
to give up

00:17:29.547 --> 00:17:31.767
-the "loving captain" act?
-It's not an act!

00:17:31.810 --> 00:17:33.638
I'm overflowing
with love and affection!

00:17:33.682 --> 00:17:35.553
-Oh, shut up!
-Youshut up!

00:17:37.947 --> 00:17:39.514
Sir, are you okay?

00:17:39.557 --> 00:17:40.950
I'll live,

00:17:40.993 --> 00:17:43.257
-but the rest of the crew...
-Will be fine.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:46.042
I initiated a rapid repeating
emergency transport sequence

00:17:46.086 --> 00:17:48.088
and beamed the entire crew
before we crashed.

00:17:48.131 --> 00:17:49.524
What? But that's not possible.

00:17:49.567 --> 00:17:51.047
No, it's a movie.
You can beam whatever you want.

00:17:51.091 --> 00:17:52.875
You can do all sorts
of beaming stuff in a movie!

00:17:52.918 --> 00:17:54.398
What?! That is amazing!

00:17:54.442 --> 00:17:56.705
-I learned it from you, sir.
-Uh... okay.

00:18:05.888 --> 00:18:07.803
What is your problem?!

00:18:07.846 --> 00:18:09.457
You've been a jerk
since I was eight!

00:18:09.500 --> 00:18:11.546
Why do you have
to be so hard on me?!

00:18:11.589 --> 00:18:13.635
What? I don't knowyou!

00:18:39.574 --> 00:18:42.751
Get off my mom, you bitch.

00:18:42.794 --> 00:18:45.623
-Oh! Wait. What?

00:18:45.667 --> 00:18:48.365
You simulated me in here, too?
Not cool, man!

00:18:48.409 --> 00:18:50.628
I got private stuff
in those logs!

00:18:50.672 --> 00:18:53.283
Emergency transport
on signal now!

00:18:53.327 --> 00:18:54.632
Beckett, no!

00:18:56.199 --> 00:18:57.983
Oh, great.
Well, now it's just us.

00:18:58.027 --> 00:18:59.724
Yeah, thanks for ruining
the awesome captain-murder

00:18:59.768 --> 00:19:01.465
this was all building to.

00:19:01.509 --> 00:19:03.946
We were supposed to fight
on a rickety metal catwalk.

00:19:03.989 --> 00:19:05.600
Oh. Let me make it up to you.
Double punch!

00:19:05.643 --> 00:19:07.384
-Double block.

00:19:07.428 --> 00:19:09.560
-Whoa. How did you...?
-I know all your moves

00:19:09.604 --> 00:19:11.432
-and everything about you.

00:19:11.475 --> 00:19:13.869
I know you dressed up
like Toby Targ every Halloween,

00:19:13.912 --> 00:19:18.003
even when you were too old.

00:19:18.047 --> 00:19:20.441
And I knowyou actually love the warp core!

00:19:20.484 --> 00:19:22.225
Take that back.
The warp core's lame!

00:19:25.097 --> 00:19:26.708
You only break rules
because you know

00:19:26.751 --> 00:19:29.537
that's what everyone expects
you to do!

00:19:29.580 --> 00:19:30.929
If you really were a badass,

00:19:30.973 --> 00:19:32.714
you'd do the hard thing
and just be

00:19:32.757 --> 00:19:34.237
a good officer.

00:19:37.240 --> 00:19:39.982
They're not casting you
as the villain. Youare!

00:19:46.293 --> 00:19:49.121
Hey, I know you might be
a psychotic space raider

00:19:49.165 --> 00:19:51.036
whose boss
just destroyed my ship,

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:53.996
but you...
are all right in my book.

00:19:54.039 --> 00:19:56.781
That's a book
I'd read cover to cover.

00:19:56.825 --> 00:19:59.915
Sir, you're the only person
who can see past my mask,

00:19:59.958 --> 00:20:01.873
and knows deep down,
I just want

00:20:01.917 --> 00:20:04.833
to replace a toranium ops modulewith ionizing subcircuits.

00:20:04.876 --> 00:20:07.052
I know this is crazy, but do youwant to just-- I don't know--

00:20:07.096 --> 00:20:09.098
run away together,
and we could get our own ship,

00:20:09.141 --> 00:20:10.882
and we can buffer the phase coilwhenever we want

00:20:10.926 --> 00:20:13.276
or... or realign the matrix.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:16.627
We can fix the warp engines
on ourtime.

00:20:16.671 --> 00:20:18.368
It would be an honor, sir.

00:20:19.674 --> 00:20:23.417
Godspeed, you crazy .

00:20:23.460 --> 00:20:25.201
Ugh. Cap'n, I knowyou've been through a lot today,

00:20:25.245 --> 00:20:27.072
but I made you a platter
of chocolate chip cookies,

00:20:27.116 --> 00:20:28.900
and I just want to know
what you think before I give it

00:20:28.944 --> 00:20:30.815
to the real you in real life,
so if you could...

00:20:30.859 --> 00:20:33.078
The captain's allergic
to chocolate. Assassin!

00:20:34.602 --> 00:20:36.168
-Great work, Jet!

00:20:36.212 --> 00:20:37.561
That's the kind
of assassin-tackling

00:20:37.605 --> 00:20:39.171
that'll land you a promotion.

00:20:39.215 --> 00:20:40.608
MAN:
Oh, hell yeah, Jet!

00:20:40.651 --> 00:20:42.305
Wait, wait. Cap'n, Cap'n,
where do you want me

00:20:42.349 --> 00:20:44.002
to see myself in five years?

00:20:44.046 --> 00:20:45.700
Don't answer that, Captain.
He's playing mind games!

00:20:45.743 --> 00:20:46.875
You're the man, Jet.

00:20:46.918 --> 00:20:48.529
-Get him out of here.
-Let's go.

00:20:48.572 --> 00:20:50.095
How can Ibe the man, Cap'n?

00:20:50.139 --> 00:20:51.619
I want to be the man!

00:21:00.889 --> 00:21:02.673
-That's it. Keep up the act.

00:21:02.717 --> 00:21:05.285
Oh, you know so much about me,

00:21:05.328 --> 00:21:07.983
but you missed one big thing.

00:21:08.026 --> 00:21:10.899
Oh, yeah, here we go-- time
for one of your snarky jokes.

00:21:10.942 --> 00:21:12.988
Yeah, I may hate protocol,

00:21:13.031 --> 00:21:15.207
but I don't hate this ship.

00:21:15.251 --> 00:21:16.818
I don't hate the crew.
I work with my best friends.

00:21:16.861 --> 00:21:19.995
The captain's my mom.
I would do anything for her.

00:21:20.038 --> 00:21:21.605
Oh, come on.
No, you hate the captain.

00:21:21.649 --> 00:21:23.172
You complain about her nonstop.

00:21:23.215 --> 00:21:24.565
It's like your whole thing!

00:21:24.608 --> 00:21:26.393
Yeah, I mean,
she's hard on me, right?

00:21:26.436 --> 00:21:28.264
She's the captain,
and I'm a pain in the ass.

00:21:28.308 --> 00:21:29.787
But if she kicked me off
the Cerritos,

00:21:29.831 --> 00:21:31.572
I would be done in Starfleet.

00:21:31.615 --> 00:21:33.922
She's watching out for me
the only way she knows how:

00:21:33.965 --> 00:21:36.141
in a  up,
overbearing, mom way.

00:21:36.185 --> 00:21:38.622
Oh, please. The only person
you care about is yourself.

00:21:41.146 --> 00:21:43.018
Okay, well, then
why did I let you kick my ass

00:21:43.061 --> 00:21:44.672
to buy time for everyone
to get off the ship

00:21:44.715 --> 00:21:47.501
before the self-destruct
timer went off?

00:21:47.544 --> 00:21:49.894
-Wait. What?

00:21:54.203 --> 00:21:57.162
No, no, no, no.
No, no, no! Aah!

00:21:57.206 --> 00:21:59.251
-No!

00:22:02.907 --> 00:22:05.649
Wow. I can't believe I just
got my ass kicked by myself

00:22:05.693 --> 00:22:07.390
and just... Wait.

00:22:07.434 --> 00:22:08.957
I guess I likeworking
on the ship and...

00:22:09.000 --> 00:22:12.177
Oh, my God. Therapy works.
Guys, therapy works!

00:22:15.485 --> 00:22:17.661
Honestly,
that was way more therapeutic

00:22:17.705 --> 00:22:19.402
than I thought it would be.
I worked through a lot.

00:22:19.446 --> 00:22:21.578
I feel great, too.
I just wish

00:22:21.622 --> 00:22:23.406
I could tell the real Billups
how I feel about him.

00:22:23.450 --> 00:22:25.103
Why don't you, man?
He's right there.

00:22:25.147 --> 00:22:27.279
Nah, I wouldn't want
to bother him. I mean,

00:22:27.323 --> 00:22:32.197
look at him.
Dude's a stone-cold badass.

00:22:32.241 --> 00:22:34.983
Hey, T.
I owe you an apology.

00:22:35.026 --> 00:22:37.115
The whole Orions-pirate thing.

00:22:37.159 --> 00:22:39.553
I-I feel really bad. I'm sorry
if I put you in a weird spot.

00:22:39.596 --> 00:22:42.077
Thanks. I appreciate it,
and the truth is,

00:22:42.120 --> 00:22:44.775
a lot of Orions are capitalist,
hyper-libertarian,

00:22:44.819 --> 00:22:47.082
gangster pirates,
just not this one.

00:22:47.125 --> 00:22:48.649
-That's why I'm here.
-Oh, well, thanks

00:22:48.692 --> 00:22:50.781
for having my back in there.
I owe you one.

00:22:50.825 --> 00:22:52.914
Um, so, do you want
to maybe go sit

00:22:52.957 --> 00:22:54.306
and look at the warp core
with me?

00:22:54.350 --> 00:22:56.352
Wow, so lame.
Yes. Let's do it.

00:22:56.396 --> 00:22:58.833
We talking warp core?
Ooh, baby, I'm in.

00:23:02.750 --> 00:23:05.448
-Mariner.
-Hey, Cap.
Sorry about earlier today.

00:23:05.492 --> 00:23:07.668
I was way out of line.
Thanks for looking out.

00:23:08.712 --> 00:23:09.931
Later, skater.

00:23:11.802 --> 00:23:14.239
"Later skater"?
I know she's up to something!

00:23:14.283 --> 00:23:15.589
What did she tell you?

00:23:15.632 --> 00:23:17.199
Captain, you know I can't share

00:23:17.242 --> 00:23:18.592
what your crew tells me.

00:23:18.635 --> 00:23:20.594
That'd be a real ethical pickle.

00:23:20.637 --> 00:23:21.986
What?!
If she's planning something,

00:23:22.030 --> 00:23:23.988
-I have a right to know.
-Carol,

00:23:24.032 --> 00:23:25.599
you're being a pineapple
right now.

00:23:25.642 --> 00:23:28.384
Ugh! Stop referencing foods!

00:23:30.386 --> 00:23:31.909
Okay. No more distractions.
I just need to know

00:23:31.953 --> 00:23:33.389
what to wear to the interview.

00:23:33.433 --> 00:23:34.782
-Computer, continue program.

00:23:34.825 --> 00:23:36.479
Hey, Cap'n,
do you like turtlenecks

00:23:36.523 --> 00:23:38.786
-or just standard uniform?
-Against insurmountable odds.

00:23:38.829 --> 00:23:40.483
Oh, sorry. You got something
going on here. I'll wait.

00:23:40.527 --> 00:23:43.268
As captain, it was an honor
serving beside her.

00:23:43.312 --> 00:23:46.794
As a mother, it was a privilege
to call Mariner my daughter.

00:23:46.837 --> 00:23:48.883
-Wait. What?
-That's right.

00:23:48.926 --> 00:23:50.667
Mariner was my daughter
the whole time.

00:23:50.711 --> 00:23:52.800
It's a secret
we didn't want anyone to know.

00:23:52.843 --> 00:23:54.454
-Uh, uh...
-And if someone had ever

00:23:54.497 --> 00:23:55.716
found out she was my baby girl,

00:23:55.759 --> 00:23:58.022
I don't know
what I would have done.

00:23:58.066 --> 00:23:59.894
Probably
kicked them off the ship,

00:23:59.937 --> 00:24:01.765
maybe even court-martialed them
right out of Starfleet.

00:24:01.809 --> 00:24:03.332
I was being crazy.

00:24:03.375 --> 00:24:04.812
-Thank goodness

00:24:04.855 --> 00:24:07.162
-nobody ever found out.
-Computer, end program!

00:24:09.773 --> 00:24:11.819
Ooh!

00:24:11.862 --> 00:24:13.516
Hey, nerd, we're going
to go stare at the warp core.

00:24:13.560 --> 00:24:15.475
You want to...?
Whoa. You okay?

00:24:15.518 --> 00:24:17.955
-: Yeah.
-All right, whatevs. Hey.

00:24:17.999 --> 00:24:20.001
Good luck with the interview.
You're gonna do great.

00:24:22.960 --> 00:24:24.396
-So, you're interested

00:24:24.440 --> 00:24:26.094
in the advanced
diplomacy workshop.

00:24:26.137 --> 00:24:28.792
Where do you see yourselfnegotiating peace in five years?

00:24:28.836 --> 00:24:30.838
I... uh...

00:24:30.881 --> 00:24:33.754
Just take a breath and say the
first thing that comes to mind.

00:24:33.797 --> 00:24:35.538
-Mariner.
-Mariner what?!

00:24:35.582 --> 00:24:38.498
-Uh... is hot?
-Excuse me?!

00:24:38.541 --> 00:24:41.631
Uh, I don't know! She's not hot!She's nasty!

00:24:45.461 --> 00:24:49.813
Ensign Boimler didn't bother toprepare for interview. Terrible.

00:25:02.260 --> 00:25:04.611
Revenge!

00:25:04.654 --> 00:25:06.569
-Not-a today.

00:25:06.613 --> 00:25:09.746
Not-a on-a da Vinci's watch.

00:26:14.289 --> 00:26:18.293
Captioned by
